window.AG_CHAPTERS["05"] = {"id":"05","title":"A-Xiu&#39;s Three Months","titleZh":"阿秀的三個月","patient":{"name":"A-Xiu 阿秀","sprite":"girl"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-clinic.jpg","key":"rain"},"pattern":"Blood Deficiency 血虛","principle":"nourish blood, and build the source that makes it","tongue":"pale body, thin white coating","pulseNote":{"en":"Fine as a thread under the finger, and it gives way when you press — there, but barely.","zh":"細如絲線，按之無力，若有若無"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>Sānyīnjiāo SP6</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"SP6","zh":"三陰交","py":"Sānyīnjiāo","x":178,"y":722,"img":"art/body-leg-medial.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"decoys":[{"x":150,"y":838},{"x":186,"y":604},{"x":196,"y":452},{"x":200,"y":286},{"x":150,"y":880}],"note":"<b>三陰交 Sānyīnjiāo SP6</b> — 3 cun above the tip of the medial malleolus, posterior to the medial border of the tibia. Meeting point of the Spleen, Liver and Kidney channels.<br>內踝尖上三寸，脛骨內側緣後方。足三陰經交會穴。"},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"Blood fails to <b>nourish</b>. Ask what is no longer being fed: the face, the eyes, the sinews, the mind, the menses.","zh":"血主濡養。當問失養之處：面色、目視、筋脈、心神、月經。"},"look":{"en":"Colour is the whole question here. Look at the tongue <b>body</b>, and at her lips and nail beds too.","zh":"此案全在一個「色」字。望舌質，並望其唇與甲床。"},"pulse":{"en":"Emptiness of blood makes the vessel narrow, not slow. Feel the <b>width</b> of the beat.","zh":"血虛則脈道不充，細而非遲。當辨其粗細。"},"dx":{"en":"Three steps: find the <b>axis</b> → check for <b>heat</b> → make tongue and pulse agree with the mechanism.","zh":"三步：找主軸 → 看寒熱 → 以舌脈校正。"},"rx":{"en":"You cannot pour from an empty jar. Nourish blood — and remember where blood is <b>made</b>.","zh":"空罐倒不出水。養血之外，勿忘血之生化之源。"},"tech":{"en":"Reinforce. And before this particular point, there is one question you must always ask a woman of childbearing age.","zh":"當用補法。且針此穴前，對育齡婦女必先問一事。"}},"reactions":[{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen watches her face, not yours. \"Go on.\"","zh":"參師父看的是她的臉，不是你的。「繼續。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"A-Xiu shifts the sleeping baby to her other arm.","zh":"阿秀把睡著的孩子換到另一隻手臂上。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy fetches a stool without being asked.","zh":"藥童沒等人吩咐就搬了張凳子來。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"She lost blood in the birth,\" he says. \"That is the beginning, not the diagnosis.\"","zh":"「她產時失血，」他說，「那是起點，不是結論。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"I keep seeing spots when I stand up,\" she says quietly.","zh":"「一站起來就眼前發黑。」她輕聲說。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Blood moistens and nourishes. Ask what has stopped being nourished.\"","zh":"「血主濡養。當問何處失其所養。」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"excess_def","look":"cold_heat","pulse":"excess_def","dx":"excess_def","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"excess_def"},"reward":{"cardEn":"Nourish the Blood","cardZh":"養血","cardTxt":"Blood that has been lost must be rebuilt, not merely moved. Nourish the blood, and strengthen the middle burner that makes it — treating only the symptom leaves the jar empty.","herbId":"danggui","herbEn":"Angelica Root","herbZh":"當歸","herbImg":"art/card-danggui.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Sweet, acrid and warm — it both nourishes blood and moves it, which is why it appears in so many gynaecological formulas."},"endings":{"three":["Six weeks on, A-Xiu comes in without holding the doorframe. \"I can see the stitches again,\" she says. \"And I sleep when the baby sleeps.\"<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You noticed the cause was loss, and you still asked what was making blood. Half of students treat only the emptiness and wonder why it returns.\"","六週後，阿秀進門時不再扶著門框。「我又看得清針腳了，」她說，「孩子睡我也能睡。」<br><b>參師父：</b>「你看見了失血這個因，卻還是問了誰在生血。一半的學生只治那個空，然後奇怪它為什麼又空回來。」"],"two":["The dizziness eases. Her sleep is still broken.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Better. One of your choices moved blood when it should have built it.\"","眩暈好些了，睡眠還是斷斷續續。<br><b>參師父：</b>「好些了。你有一步是行血，而那時該生血。」"],"one":["A-Xiu is no better, and more tired for the walk.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Look at her lips again. Colour was telling you everything, and you looked past it.\"","阿秀沒有起色，反因走這一趟更累。<br><b>參師父：</b>「再看一次她的唇。顏色早就把話說盡了，你卻看過去了。」"],"titles":["A-Xiu Sees Clearly Again","A-Xiu Sleeps a Little","A-Xiu Will Need Another Visit"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"Last time you learned to build before you drain. Today the loss is not slow. It happened in one night.","cn":"上次你學會了先補而後利。今天這個虛，不是慢慢來的。它是一夜之間的事。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Doctor. I'm A-Xiu. My daughter is three months old. I bled a great deal at the birth.","cn":"大夫。我是阿秀，女兒三個月大。生的時候血崩過。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Since then my head swims when I stand. My heart races at night and I can't fall asleep, even when I'm exhausted.","cn":"從那以後，一起身就頭暈。夜裡心慌，累得要死也睡不著。"},{"w":"master","en":"Blood moistens the body and houses the spirit. When it is short, both suffer — and they suffer together.","cn":"血主濡養，又舍神。血不足則二者俱病，且是一起病。"},{"w":"master","en":"Do not stop at 'she lost blood'. Ask what is no longer being nourished. That is where the pattern lives.","cn":"不要停在「她失了血」。要問何處失養——證就在那裡。"}],"qa":[{"q":"What is your complexion like, and your lips and nails?","cq":"面色如何？唇與指甲呢？","good":1,"a":"My mother-in-law says I've gone the colour of paper. My lips look washed out to me.","ca":"婆婆說我臉白得像紙。我自己看嘴唇也是淡的。","clue":{"en":"Pale complexion, pale lips and nails","zh":"面色淡白、唇甲色淡"},"note":"Blood shows itself in colour. A pale face with pale lips and nail beds is the plainest sign that blood is not reaching the surface. 血之榮枯見於色。面唇甲俱淡，血不上榮之明證。"},{"q":"How is your vision, and are your hands or feet numb?","cq":"視物如何？手足會麻嗎？","good":1,"a":"Things blur when I sew. And my fingers go numb, especially at night.","ca":"做針線就看不清。手指會麻，晚上尤其。","clue":{"en":"Blurred vision, numb limbs","zh":"目視昏花、肢麻"},"note":"The Liver stores blood, opens into the eyes and rules the sinews. Blurred vision and numb limbs are those two functions starved at once. 肝藏血、開竅於目、主筋。目昏肢麻，即此二者失養。"},{"q":"Do your calves cramp at night?","cq":"夜裡小腿會抽筋嗎？","good":1,"a":"Yes — it wakes me. I have to stand on the cold floor until it passes.","ca":"會，痛醒。得下床踩冷地板才緩得過來。","clue":{"en":"Night cramps in the calves","zh":"夜間腓腸拘攣"},"note":"Blood returns to the Liver at night, and the sinews are left short. Night cramping with pale nails is blood deficiency, not cold. 夜臥血歸於肝，筋失所養而攣。夜間抽筋兼甲淡，屬血虛非寒。"},{"q":"Since the birth, have your periods returned? What are they like?","cq":"產後月經來了嗎？量色如何？","good":1,"a":"Once, last month. Very little, and pale. It came late.","ca":"上個月來過一次。量很少，顏色淡，而且遲了。","clue":{"en":"Scanty pale delayed menses","zh":"經少色淡、延後"},"note":"Scanty, pale, delayed menses is the gynaecological signature of blood deficiency. Heavy bright-red would mean heat; dark with clots would mean stasis or cold. 經少、色淡、延後，血虛之婦科主症。量多鮮紅屬熱；暗而有塊屬瘀或寒。"},{"q":"Do you have hot flushes, night sweats, or heat in your palms and soles?","cq":"有沒有潮熱、盜汗、五心煩熱？","good":1,"a":"No, none of that. If anything I feel cold.","ca":"沒有。真要說，我是覺得冷。","clue":{"en":"No heat signs","zh":"無虛熱象"},"note":"The exclusion that separates blood deficiency from <b>Yin deficiency</b>. Both are empty, but yin deficiency generates heat — tidal fever, night sweats, five-centre heat. She has none. 此問分血虛與陰虛。二者皆虛，然陰虛生內熱：潮熱、盜汗、五心煩熱。本案皆無。"},{"q":"Is there fixed stabbing pain anywhere that worsens at night?","cq":"有沒有固定刺痛、夜間加重？","good":0,"a":"No. Nothing hurts like that.","ca":"沒有那種痛。","clue":"","note":"A sound exclusion, but negative. Fixed stabbing pain worse at night with a purple tongue would be <b>blood stasis</b> — a different problem with the same word in it. 排除得當，惟為陰性。固定刺痛、夜甚、舌紫，乃血瘀，與血虛同字而異證。"}],"look":[{"t":"Pale tongue body, thin white coat","c":"舌質淡，苔薄白","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Pale tongue","zh":"舌淡"},"note":"Correct. The tongue body reflects blood and the organs behind it; a pale body with a normal thin coat says the blood is short but no pathogen has formed. 舌質候血與臟腑。質淡而苔薄白，血不足而無邪。"},{"t":"Pale, swollen body with tooth marks","c":"舌淡胖、有齒痕","ok":0,"note":"That is qi deficiency with damp — the previous patient's tongue. Hers is pale but not swollen: blood is thin, fluid is not pooling. 此為氣虛濕停，乃前案之舌。本案淡而不胖：血少，非水停。"},{"t":"Dark purple body with stasis spots","c":"舌紫暗、有瘀點","ok":0,"note":"Blood stasis. Stasis is blood that cannot move; hers is blood that is not there. 此為血瘀。瘀者血行不暢，虛者血本不足。"},{"t":"Red body with little coat, dry","c":"舌紅少苔而乾","ok":0,"note":"Yin deficiency with empty heat. She has no heat signs at all, and a red tongue would contradict every other finding. 此為陰虛內熱。本案通身無熱象，舌紅則與諸症相悖。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Thready and weak 細弱","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Thready weak pulse","zh":"脈細弱"},"note":"Correct. Thready means the vessel is narrow — not enough blood to fill it. Weak adds that there is no force behind it. 細者脈道不充，血少也；弱者無力，氣亦不足以鼓之。"},{"t":"Choppy 澀","ok":0,"note":"A choppy pulse means blood moving with difficulty — stasis. Hers moves freely; there is simply little of it. 澀主血行不利，乃瘀。本案血行無阻，惟血少耳。"},{"t":"Rapid and thready 細數","ok":0,"note":"Rapid adds heat. That reading belongs to yin deficiency with empty heat — and she has no heat anywhere. 數則兼熱，屬陰虛內熱。本案無熱。"},{"t":"Deep and slow 沉遲","ok":0,"note":"Deep and slow is cold. Cold in the blood brings cold cramping pain relieved by warmth, which she does not have. 沉遲主寒。血寒者冷痛得溫則減，本案不然。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — find the axis. Which is the leading disorder?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：找主軸。何者為主病？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Deficiency of blood — nourishing has failed","c":"血虛 — 濡養失職","ok":1,"note":"Pale face, lips and nails; blurred vision; numb limbs; night cramps; scanty pale menses; palpitations and insomnia. Every one of those is a tissue no longer being fed. 面唇甲淡、目昏、肢麻、夜攣、經少色淡、心悸失眠——無一不是失養。"},{"t":"Qi stagnation — movement is blocked","c":"氣滯 — 氣機不暢","ok":0,"note":"Stagnation gives distension and wandering pain that shifts with mood and eases after belching or passing wind. She has no distension at all. 氣滯主脹、走竄、隨情志起伏、噯氣矢氣則減。本案無脹。"},{"t":"Blood stasis — blood cannot move","c":"血瘀 — 血行不暢","ok":0,"note":"Stasis gives fixed stabbing pain, worse at night, a purple tongue and a choppy pulse. Her tongue is pale and her pulse is thready. 瘀者固定刺痛、夜甚、舌紫、脈澀。本案舌淡脈細。"},{"t":"Fluid deficiency — dryness leads","c":"津虧 — 以燥為主","ok":0,"note":"Fluid deficiency leads with dryness of mouth, nose, throat and stool. Her skin is dry, but the leading signs are colour and nourishment, not dryness. 津虧以口鼻咽燥、便乾為主。本案膚雖乾，主症在色與失養，非燥。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — is there heat?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：看寒熱。</small>","opts":[{"t":"No heat — this is emptiness without fire","c":"無熱 — 純虛無火","ok":1,"note":"This is the fork that separates blood deficiency from yin deficiency, and it decides the whole treatment. No tidal fever, no night sweats, no five-centre heat, tongue pale not red, pulse thready but not rapid. 此為血虛與陰虛之分水嶺，關乎全局。無潮熱、無盜汗、無五心煩熱；舌淡不紅，脈細不數。"},{"t":"Yes — empty heat from yin deficiency","c":"有 — 陰虛內熱","ok":0,"note":"Then you would expect tidal fever, night sweats, heat in the palms and soles, a red tongue with little coat, and a thready rapid pulse. Not one of those is present. 當見潮熱、盜汗、五心煩熱、舌紅少苔、脈細數。本案無一符合。"},{"t":"Yes — heat is driving the blood","c":"有 — 血熱妄行","ok":0,"note":"Blood heat shows as bright red heavy bleeding with fever and thirst. Her menses are scanty and pale — the opposite reading. 血熱則出血鮮紅量多，兼身熱口渴。本案經少色淡，恰恰相反。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — make tongue and pulse agree with the mechanism.<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：以舌脈校正。</small>","opts":[{"t":"Pale tongue and thready weak pulse — both say the vessel is under-filled","c":"舌淡、脈細弱 — 皆言脈道不充","ok":1,"note":"Symptoms, tongue and pulse must all be explainable by one mechanism. Here they are: not enough blood to colour the tissue, and not enough to fill the vessel. When they contradict each other, you have missed a layer or asked the wrong question. 症、舌、脈須以同一病機貫之。此案皆通：血不足以榮色，亦不足以充脈。若三者相悖，則有兼證，或問診有失。"},{"t":"The pulse is decisive; the tongue can be ignored here","c":"以脈為斷，舌可不論","ok":0,"note":"Never. A single axis can mislead — a thready pulse alone appears in yin deficiency too. It is the <b>agreement</b> of the three that confirms a pattern. 不可。單憑一診易誤：脈細亦見於陰虛。三者相合，證乃可定。"},{"t":"They disagree, so this must be a mixed pattern","c":"三者不合，當屬兼證","ok":0,"note":"They do not disagree. Pale body and thready weak pulse point the same way. Reach for a mixed pattern only when the evidence genuinely pulls in two directions. 並無不合。舌淡與脈細弱同指一機。惟證據確實分歧時，方論兼證。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"SP6","t":"Sānyīnjiāo SP6 三陰交","ok":1,"note":"Where the Spleen, Liver and Kidney channels cross — one needle reaching the organ that makes blood, the organ that stores it, and the organ that governs reproduction. The first point of almost every gynaecological prescription. 脾肝腎三經交會：一針而及生血之臟、藏血之臟、主生殖之臟。婦科方之首選。"},{"id":"ST36","t":"Zúsānlǐ ST36 足三里","ok":1,"note":"Blood is made from food and drink in the middle burner. Nourishing blood without strengthening its source empties again as soon as you stop. 氣血生化於中焦水穀。養血而不健其源，停治即復虛。"},{"id":"SP10","t":"Xuèhǎi SP10 血海","ok":1,"note":"The Sea of Blood. Its name is its indication — it both nourishes and moves blood, and belongs in almost any blood pattern of the lower burner. 血海，名即其用。養血兼活血，下焦血證多用之。"},{"id":"LR3","t":"Tàichōng LR3 太衝","ok":0,"note":"Moves stuck Liver qi — and there is nothing stuck. Moving a depleted patient spends the little she has. Reach for it when blood deficiency has knotted into constraint, not before. 疏肝行氣，然本案無鬱。虛而行之，是耗其所餘。俟血虛致鬱，方可用之。"},{"id":"SP9","t":"Yīnlíngquán SP9 陰陵泉","ok":0,"note":"Drains damp. There is no damp here — no greasy coat, no heaviness, no loose stool. Draining an empty patient is the mistake this whole sequence of chapters is teaching you to stop making. 利濕之穴，然本案無濕：苔不膩、身不重、便不溏。虛者而瀉之，正是前後數章所戒。"},{"id":"LU7","t":"Lièquē LU7 列缺","ok":0,"note":"Releases the exterior. Her illness began inside, from loss, three months ago. 解表之穴。本案病起於內，因失血，已三月。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Reinforcing method, gentle needling, moxa welcome — and confirm she is not pregnant again","c":"補法，手法宜輕，可施灸 — 並須確認未再受孕","ok":1,"note":"Correct on both counts. An empty pattern is reinforced gently, and warmth suits a patient who feels cold. And SP6 is <b>contraindicated in pregnancy</b> — she is three months postpartum, not pregnant, but the question is asked <i>every time</i>, of every woman of childbearing age, before this point is used. Habit is what makes a caution reliable. 二者皆是。虛則補之，手法宜輕；其人畏冷，兼可施灸。三陰交孕婦禁針——本案產後三月非孕，然此問當每次必問，對每一育齡婦女皆然。禁忌之所以可靠，在於成習慣。"},{"t":"Reinforcing method, and no need to ask about pregnancy since she just gave birth","c":"補法即可；方才生產，無須再問是否懷孕","ok":0,"note":"The method is right and the reasoning is dangerous. Conception can occur before the first postpartum period returns. SP6 and LI4 are asked about every single time — that is precisely why they are safe points in practice. 手法無誤，而理路危險。產後首次月經之前即可能受孕。三陰交、合谷每次必問，此其所以安全。"},{"t":"Reducing method with strong stimulation to break through","c":"瀉法重刺激以通其滯","ok":0,"note":"There is nothing to break through, and she has nothing to spare. 無滯可通，亦無餘可耗。"},{"t":"Bleed the well points to bring blood to the surface","c":"點刺井穴引血外達","ok":0,"note":"Bleeding removes blood from a patient who is short of it. This is the one thing you must not do here. 刺血是奪其血，於血虛者為大忌。"}]};
